{# The arrow of a navigation control, wherever one is drawn.

   Thirty-two of these were written by hand across fifteen templates, each one
   a `<path>` nobody could change without editing Twig. They are the same
   object: a chevron saying which way something moves. One place decides what
   it looks like, and the theme decides once for the whole site.

   Expected variables:
     - direction : 'next' | 'prev' | 'up' | 'down' (default 'next')
     - role      : 'control' | 'chevron' (default 'control')
     - class     : extra classes for the svg

   Two roles, two settings, because they are not the same object. A control is
   the button that moves a carousel or a page: it acts, it is big, it can be a
   circled arrow. A chevron only says that something opens or leads somewhere -
   at the end of a list row, beside a menu entry - and the same circled arrow
   would be absurd there. The breadcrumb separator is a third thing again and
   takes neither: it marks hierarchy between two names, and has its own setting.

   Between them they are still one decision each, made once for the whole site.

   What it draws is the pictogram pair the whole bundle offers - one from the
   theme library, or one of the project's own from the media library - so the
   arrows are set up exactly like the pictogram of a button or of a card, down
   to the size. `_icon.html.twig` already knows how to draw that pair, mask an
   SVG so it takes the surrounding colour, and size it, so the settings are
   handed to it as the item it expects.

   The direction is a class, `iw-nav-arrow--prev` and friends, which the
   stylesheet turns. It is applied as a rotation rather than as a second
   choice: a person setting up a theme picks one arrow, not four that have to
   agree with each other, and a pictogram with no direction of its own - a dot,
   a cross - still works, it simply turns.

   With nothing set, the chevron below is the one these templates already drew,
   so a site that never opens the setting does not move. #}

{%- set direction = direction|default('next') -%}

{%- set role = role|default('control') -%}

{%- if 'chevron' == role -%}
    {%- set arrowCustom = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsChevronIconCustom|default(false) -%}
    {%- set arrowIcon = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsChevronIcon|default('') -%}
    {%- set arrowMedia = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsChevronIconMedia|default(null) -%}
    {%- set arrowSize = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsChevronIconSize|default('') -%}
{%- else -%}
    {%- set arrowCustom = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsArrowIconCustom|default(false) -%}
    {%- set arrowIcon = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsArrowIcon|default('') -%}
    {%- set arrowMedia = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsArrowIconMedia|default(null) -%}
    {%- set arrowSize = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.components_controlsArrowIconSize|default('') -%}
{%- endif -%}

{#- Callers pass the size they have always drawn at, as utility classes. Those
    weigh the same as the one carrying the chosen size, so the later of the two
    in the stylesheet would win and a size set in the admin would be ignored
    here and obeyed elsewhere. When a size is set, they step aside. -#}
{%- set callerClass = class|default('') -%}
{%- if arrowSize -%}
    {%- set callerClass = callerClass|split(' ')|filter(c => c starts with 'w-' or c starts with 'h-' ? false : true)|join(' ') -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set arrowClass = ('iw-nav-arrow iw-nav-arrow--' ~ direction ~ ' ' ~ callerClass)|trim -%}

{%- set hasArrow = arrowCustom ? (arrowMedia is not null) : (arrowIcon is not empty) -%}

{%- if hasArrow %}
    {#- An arrow is a sign, not a picture of the project: a custom SVG takes the
        colour around it like a library one does, hence `recolor`. -#}
    {% include '@ItechWorldSuluTailwindTheme/blocks/common/_icon.html.twig' with {
        'item': {
            'iconCustom': arrowCustom,
            'icon': arrowIcon,
            'iconMedia': arrowMedia,
            'iconSize': arrowSize,
        },
        'class': arrowClass,
        'recolor': true,
    } only %}
{%- else %}
    <svg class="{{ arrowClass }}" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/>
    </svg>
{%- endif %}
